4021

; Introduction -------------------------------------------------------------

BEGINTEXT


    "Civilization, as Empire scholars would define it, in the Kellandra
    Sector appears  to have begun only  when the First Empire  extended
    it's reach this far out.  The idyllic planets that cover  this area
    seem to have given the populations  no incentive to leave.  Most of
    the native lifeforms never developed space travel even at the level
    of the warp fighters we now consider  primitive.  This allowed  the
    First Empire easy  expansion, and quickly lead to  the discovery of    
    of the valuble resources in the central core of the sector."

                              -Jairius Azrai'le, Dean of Anthropology
                               Skool University, Library of Antiquity 
                               About 1250 years before the Collapse

    "The fall of Civilization in this sector gives an interesting proof
    of my previously described theories.  Civilization appears to  have
    collapsed first at  the Periphery, that part of the region that has    

NEWPAGE

    an abnormally high amount of planets that  are perfectly suited for
    human life. This was due not to violent revolt, but to a very quiet
    and  bloodless coup.   The Rim planets, when the Empire fell,  were
    free to throw off the technological shackles that were imposed upon
    upon them.  Most planets  reverted to their previous levels or even
    lower.  It follows from my theories that the Center worlds with the
    harsher enviroments will retain their technology.  Whether they can
    advance or not is up to time and remains to be seen."

                              -Lanthone Asrae'la, Head of Social Science
                               Skool University, Modern Publication, v84
                               Year 2520 Post-Collapse

NEWPAGE

    The world you inhabit is just beginning to discover space travel. A
    few intellectuals turned to the task after indications of others in
    the Galaxy were  discovered.  The expended probe was recovered  and
    given to the schools. In a few decades, a fighter defense force was
    established  and thoughts turned to  exploring the universe  around
    your world.  A transport  fleet was constructed  in short order and
    that is where your rule begins. You know there is someone out there
    and they might know you're out there.  Expand into the universe and
    perhaps meet them on their own terms, or stay on your beautiful and
    peacful planet and perhaps they will find you...  
     
ENDTEXT

BEGINDESCRIPTION

