TEXT 1

A pardise, this planet, happy for millenia to merely live free and happy.
That peace is now threatened by the reality that you are not alone in this
universe.  Your civilization, forced to leave it's cradle, is in for a 
very rude awakening.

Recommended Victory Conditions: Last surviving empire or a member of the
                                last remaining coalition. 

ENDTEXT

TEXT 2

A fairly hospitible world for this region of space, it has maintained it's
own little empire through generations of very strong rulers and an inward-
looking philosophy. A monarchy, but a meritocratic one, it's well-trained 
leaders are all that keeps it from collapsing into anarchy, that and the
ruler's single-handed control of an ancient terror weapon.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 3

The capital of a loosely allied coalition of planets, this planet is the 
nominal head of the empire.  Retaining some, but not all of the technology
from the times of the First Empire, it makes use of this to expand it's 
territory.  Their expansion is aided by the presence of a space-based
factory.     

ENDTEXT

TEXT 4

This planet leads an empire that rose from the remains of the First.  It 
is a forward-thinking empire that spares a world to research the ancient
technologies.  It has also found a way to refine a drug common on the 
Periphery, making large amounts of it available to it's populace.  While
it doesn't use these two worlds to make ships, it's expansion is not 
hindered; it is large enough to have many ship bases.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 5

Called "Protheos", this planet was a jumpship base for the old Empire.  It
is a gas giant, a perfect ship base; it is even now producing limited amount
of ships for that is all it's people know.  Somewhere, around this planet 
is the last shipment the planet was to deliver to the Empire, it has been
moth-balled and, perhaps, the ships are still able to function.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 6

Now known only to the scholars that inhabit the planet, "Skool" was the 
Empire's university before the Collapse.  After the Collapse, they have
assumed the task of keeping the knowledge alive.  However, they realized
that perhaps this sector was better off without that knowlegde.  Because
of this they created extensive, automated defenses, the few ships that
remain are used primarily as teaching aids and most wouldn't function
in combat anymore.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 7

A world hostile to human life, "Nilon", seemed the perfect palce to train
the Empire's elite troops.  Extensive use was made of these during the last 
death throes of the First Empire.  They were and, in places, are remebered
vividly.  For this reason they try to hide their existance; this is even 
more important since the Empire left them with only a small fleet, mainly
troop tranports.  The amount of ninjas on the planet is low, because their
training requires a rare drug and precious little remains.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 8

An almost perfect planet, "Eden" is home to a remarkably large population
for a primitive world.  People accidently stumble upon the planet and can't
believe their eyes.  Named after ancient legends, it lives up to the dreams.
Most crews abandon their ships in orbit and are welcomed into the society
with open arms.  A few that would attack find the population unwilling to
be coerced to work, and most conquerors quickly leave or are converted.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 9

A wonder of ancient engineering, "Dyson" is not a planet but an artificial
sphere containing it's own yellow sun.  Completed under the old Empire, it
has decayed over the years due to lack of repair, but it is still one of 
the universe's treasures.  Home to a quarter of a trillion people, this
world remeber's the past and does not wish to be conquered again.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 10

Before the Collapse, Imperial scientists spent a lot of time and effort
observing this one blue-green planet.  While it is now very primitive and
sparsely populated, records found in Empire libraries and artifacts found
here seem to point towards this planet being the homeworld of the human 
race.  This cannot be confirmed for those times are lost to legend, but the
hope was enough to keep the Empire observation teams here until the end.

ENDTEXT

TEXT 11

You have conquered the Old Empire's sector capital; it's empire crumbles.
If you have taken this world, perhaps you still have the strength to pick
up the pieces and bring them under your rule.  With them the Galaxy, could
be united again, with your flag...

ENDTEXT

TEXT 12

This star fortress was once used by the Empire to exert it's control over 
this whole sector.  Kellandra uses it much the same way, if more limited
in scope.  If it was yours...

ENDTEXT 

ENDDESCRIPTION    

    

